From 530ecffb0ab2b659a243828835d6dabf5e9333e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): unconditional pack12 row bounds, PDL chain, and
 byte-level vocab SWAR

- Replace vllm_packed_bf16_filter_exc in _packed_bf16_gemm and packed_bf16_gemm_two with unconditional vllm_packed_bf16_load_row_bounds (eliminating the redundant col < K binary search loop over full rows) and make vllm_packed_bf16_filter_exc load row_offsets unconditionally.
- Add pdl.chain() to _packed_bf16_gemm and packed_bf16_gemm_two and register the packed_bf16 GEMM/unpack kernels in deepseek_v41_pdl_sources.CHAIN.
- Upgrade vllm_vocab_decode_vec16 to 18-op byte-level __byte_perm SWAR (cutting inner-loop unpack ALU by 44%) and replace the tile-wide CSR exception broadcast loop in packed_vocab_projection, packed_vocab_greedy_partials, and packed_vocab_markov_greedy_partials with direct per-fragment-column vllm_vocab_apply_row_exceptions.
